  "title": "tls-utils: Don't allocate memory for hash if the tvb doesn't have it",
  "description": "Check to see if the tvb passed in actually has the bytes to be added\nto the hash before reallocing additional memory for it. Also handle\nthe edge case used in TLS to add a few null bytes when calculating\nthe hash as though each message was sent in a single fragment.\n\nFix #18903",
